 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "Cargo.toml:14; crates/sc-config/Cargo.toml:3; crates/sc-transport/Cargo.toml:3; docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-3-runtime-ecosystem-upgrade.md:175; docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-3-runtime-ecosystem-upgrade.md:203; docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-3-runtime-ecosystem-upgrade.md:400; tests/unit/generation/test_runtime_ecosystem_upgrade.py:84" ;
 triage:issue "The pushed C3 contract and manifest/tests still freeze only four public packages at0.2.0 and require config/transport0.1.1 plus selective-publisher qualification. This contradicts the superseding all-six-public-crates release policy. The C4 handoff still describes fixed schema/duplicate defects as unresolved and supplies the superseded selective contract, so its release-input gate is not closed." ;
 triage:action "Align all six public packages and their normal/dev/template edges to the shared0.2.0 release, update the governing version matrix/phase/sprint/handoff and exact assertions, and prepare the existing-kit all-crates prepublication handoff. Preserve historical evidence and SQLite third-party pins. Do not implement a selective kit enhancement; C4 still owns publication and registry proof." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

