 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/Cargo.toml:29; crates/sc-runtime/src/mcp_input.rs:40; boundaries/sc-runtime/sc-runtime.toml:35; docs/sc-runtime/architecture.md:367" ;
 triage:issue "The private duplicate-key guard adds serde_json as a normal dependency and amends the boundary/architecture, but NFR-RT-0003 still says the normal dependency set is exactly its listed table, which excludes serde_json. Implementation authorization is not a committed normative requirement amendment." ;
 triage:action "Reconcile the owning exact dependency requirement with the reviewed private-input design and mirror the same allowed edge consistently, or implement the required behavior without the extra edge. Preserve ordinary consumer MCP composition and its configured body limit." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_REQ_C3_005 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C3-005" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/tests/phase_c_hooks.rs:66; crates/sc-runtime/src/tests/phase_c_hooks.rs:96" ;
 triage:issue "The new prebind-order regression awaits dropped.await without any failure bound; precisely the regression it tests (retaining the unused stores sender until after cleanup) leaves run and the test waiting forever. The reserve/drop negative also assumes immediate rebind of a released ephemeral port succeeds; another simultaneous suite can bind that released port between lines70 and71, making this an OS-scheduling race." ;
 triage:action "Redesign these negative proofs with causal synchronization and bounded accurate failure paths. A broken unused-closure order must fail and reclaim ownership rather than hang. Prove the planted endpoint-ownership defect without assuming exclusive ownership of a port after releasing its listener; do not add retries, skips, serialization, or larger timeouts." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

