 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/testing.rs:48" ;
 triage:issue "The test-util module publicly exports the free function instrument_router, while NFR-RT-0001 closes the public surface to its listed items and explicitly forbids any public free function. No documented test-helper exception exists. This is inherited but remains in C3's owned testing surface." ;
 triage:action "Reconcile this useful test helper with the closed public surface: remove the unapproved free export or make an explicit planned/reviewed normative surface amendment. Keep production builder/typestate and feature isolation unchanged." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_REQ_C3_007 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C3-007" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/tests/windows_console.rs:114; crates/sc-runtime/tests/windows_console.rs:119; crates/sc-runtime/tests/windows_console_driver.py:148" ;
 triage:issue "The Python controller checks the full isolated-runner marker set, but the separately invocable Rust console_child test checks only SC_RUNTIME_EPHEMERAL_CI after its child selector. Direct selection with those two custom variables can enter the daemon path on a developer host without the required GITHUB_ACTIONS/github-hosted checks. The rule requires each daemon-process test to refuse before spawning/running the daemon, not only its preferred controller." ;
 triage:action "Apply the same fail-closed isolated-runner guard at the Rust child entry before runtime/daemon creation, preferably shared with the controller contract, and test that partial/mismatched marker sets cannot start a daemon." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

