triage:C3_QA1_RSH_C3_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "RSH-C3-001" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "rust-service-hardening-agent" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/router.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Request/drain timeout recovery instructs callers to replay a potentially committed mutation. A timeout only drops the polled handler future; already admitted blocking/owned work may finish and commit afterwards. Both wire suggestions and request.error diagnostic say to retry, contradicting the uncertain-outcome compatibility contract and exposing integrators to duplicate effects." ;
 triage:action "Keep stable 503/error codes, but make wire and canonical-log recovery value-free and outcome-aware: completion may be unknown; reconcile through separately authorized reads before considering any replay. Document that cancellation cannot prove rollback. Add a causal middleware regression with admitted owned work completing after the response and assert no blanket retry guidance." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_RSH_C3_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "RSH-C3-002" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "rust-service-hardening-agent" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/mcp_input.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The new ingress validator recursively rejects duplicate keys in every JSON object, including opaque application payloads and unrelated consumer MCP tools. The canonical cron DTO uses serde_json::Value for payload, so CLI/HTTP accept an opaque object with repeated keys using Value semantics while MCP rejects the identical request before the executor. This silently changes the consumer-owned arbitrary JSON input contract and shared UI semantics." ;
 triage:action "Preserve configured byte bounds and exact request parts/deadline, but enforce strict duplicate rules at the governed protocol/DTO struct fields without imposing extra semantics on opaque payload objects or arbitrary consumer tools. Add actual CLI/HTTP/MCP parity coverage for duplicates inside opaque payload alongside negative duplicate struct-field cases." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-001" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/tests/phase_c_hooks.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The cleanup-order negative hangs on the exact regression it should reject. If run_with_cleanup_and_bound keeps the unused stores closure alive until cleanup returns, cleanup waits forever for its captured oneshot sender to be dropped; the sender cannot drop until that same cleanup finishes. Neither the cleanup await nor the outer run has a deadline." ;
 triage:action "Use a synchronous drop-state witness (for example a Drop flag and immediate assertion/try_recv) at the cleanup boundary instead of waiting for the event whose ordering is under test. Keep any adversarial fixture physically supervised if it must exercise uncooperative work. Do not hide the deadlock with retries or a larger timeout." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-002" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/tests/phase_c_hooks.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Dropping the reservation before the second bind exposes the chosen ephemeral port to every concurrent local binder. Another test/process can acquire it in that gap, so the second bind panics despite correct production behavior. This negative test introduces the very reserve/drop race that the real retained-listener hook removes." ;
 triage:action "Retire the naked-port negative or replace it with a controlled ownership/double boundary that proves release causally. Keep the production callback test which attempts a competing bind while the actual listener remains owned. Do not retry the bind, serialize tests, or pad a delay." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-003" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-runtime/src/testing.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The negative assertion for early join/detach is a 50ms scheduling sample, without a witness that the joiner actually entered the join operation. A broken join/drop implementation can pass if its thread is descheduled until after is_finished is sampled; the test then releases the held thread and sees the expected final state. held_thread also uses deadline-free receiver waits, and the parent joins are deadline-free." ;
 triage:action "Redesign the test around causal entry/ownership witnesses rather than sleep/is_finished. Use bounded acknowledgements for held-thread readiness, and supervise any case whose intentionally broken join can stall the process, retaining physical cleanup ownership. Do not increase 50ms or serialize execution." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-004" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "examples/spike/phase-c-contract/probe.py" ;
 triage:issue "The committed executable qualification probes call subprocess.run with captured pipes and no deadline or process-tree owner. A blocked cargo/lint subprocess or descendant holding an inherited pipe can indefinitely block the probe, even after the direct process exits." ;
 triage:action "Remove these temporary qualification executables from the deliverable if their evidence is already recorded, or use the canonical bounded owned-process runner with file capture and physical descendant cleanup. A timeout on only the immediate process is insufficient." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_005 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-005" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_unix.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Inspector failure returns before the owned direct launcher is reaped. Drop retries the failed stop then only sends start_kill, releasing the ChildWrapper without proving physical completion. A cleanup failure can therefore return while the direct owned child remains alive or unreaped." ;
 triage:action "Preserve the inspection failure but complete bounded direct-leader kill/reap on every inspector spawn/status/deadline error before releasing ownership. Keep descendant/session cleanup and the original deadline; add a causal failed-inspector return-boundary witness." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .

triage:C3_QA1_FTQ_C3_006 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C3-006" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "81147f025a356ea72caf17439c38b10c4d9d7627" ;
 triage:file "tests/integration/generation/owned_process.py" ;
 triage:issue "The inner Python Windows owner treats empty JobObject accounting as complete descendant termination. Job active accounting may reach zero before a terminated process object becomes signaled; waiting only on the launcher does not close this interval for other descendants. Consequently run can return and the console/projection test can release temporary state while descendants still physically execute termination. The outer Rust owner repairs this for its own return, but does not make this Python helper independently safe or prevent a following inner scenario racing cleanup." ;
 triage:action "Retain actual member process identities before termination, then require their completion signals as well as zero active accounting and launcher reap before returning. Share the existing canonical repair and deterministic empty-job/unsignaled-member witness; do not add a post-kill sleep." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/120#issuecomment-6649171633" .
